---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="A chained hash table with a fixed number of buckets: insert every key, then look every key up once. A probe is one key compared while walking a chain. Time is an assumed cost per probe, nothing is timed on your machine.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with the defaults, a good hash, <b>Number of buckets</b> <b>16,384</b>, <b>Number of keys</b> <b>10,000</b> and random keys: the load factor is <b>0.61</b>, keys spread over <b>7,520</b> buckets, the longest chain is <b>6</b> and a lookup compares <b>1.29</b> keys. The whole request is <b>15,968</b> probes.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Hash function</b> to "Poor: last digit only": the same keys fill only <b>10</b> buckets, the longest chain is <b>1,000</b> and the request makes <b>10,000,000</b> probes. Then set <b>Hash function</b> back to "Good, known to the attacker" and <b>Number of buckets</b> to <b>16</b>: the hash is fine but the table is simply too small: <b>313.34</b> probes per lookup.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Hash function</b> to "Good, known to the attacker", <b>Number of buckets</b> to <b>16,384</b> and <b>Key pattern</b> to "Attacker-chosen": all keys share one bucket, <b>100,000,000</b> probes, which is <b>6,263</b> times the cost of honest keys, and <b>1</b> s at 10 ns per probe.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Hash function</b> to "Good, with a secret seed": the same attacker keys now cost <b>16,034</b> probes and the longest chain is <b>5</b>.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg ht" data-ht>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Hash function <select class="pg-in" data-fn><option value="good" selected>Good, known to the attacker</option><option value="seeded">Good, with a secret seed</option><option value="poor">Poor: last digit only</option><option value="constant">Constant (always bucket 0)</option></select></label>
      <label>Number of buckets <select class="pg-in" data-m><option value="16">16</option><option value="128">128</option><option value="1024">1,024</option><option value="16384" selected>16,384</option></select></label>
      <label>Number of keys <select class="pg-in" data-n><option value="100">100</option><option value="1000">1,000</option><option value="10000" selected>10,000</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Key pattern <select class="pg-in" data-pattern><option value="random" selected>Random</option><option value="sequential">Sequential</option><option value="adversarial">Attacker-chosen</option></select></label>
      <label>Cost per probe <select class="pg-in" data-cost><option value="10" selected>10 ns</option><option value="100">100 ns</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Load factor</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-lf></span><span class="pg-note" data-lfn></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-lbox><h3>Longest chain</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-longest></span><span class="pg-note" data-used></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-abox><h3>Probes per lookup</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-avg></span><span class="pg-note">average, for the keys that were inserted</span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-tbox><h3>Total probes</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-total></span><span class="pg-note" data-time></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Bucket sizes, largest first</h3>
      <svg class="ht-chart" data-chart viewBox="0 0 600 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-label="Size of the 60 largest buckets"></svg>
      <span class="pg-note" data-axis></span>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" data-dos><h3>Compared with honest keys</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-dosn></span><span class="pg-note" data-dost></span></div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict role="status"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: the table has a fixed number of buckets (a real one would resize, see amortized analysis); keys are 32-bit numbers; "good" is multiplicative hashing, and the seeded version stands in for a keyed hash such as SipHash. The attacker knows the unseeded hash: for "Good" they send keys whose hash is 0, for "Poor" keys ending in 0, and against a constant hash anything works. A secret seed cannot rescue a poor or constant hash. Fixed key generator, so results repeat.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, formatThousands, formatOneDecimalBelow100 } from '../playground';
  const MULT = 2654435761, MULT_INV = 244002641, MIX = 2246822519, SEED = 2718281828;
  const SHOWN = 60;
  // Same model as the code samples: bucket choice, key generators and probe counting.
  function bucketOf(fn: string, key: number, m: number): number {
    if (fn === 'constant') return 0;
    if (fn === 'poor') return (key % 10) % m;
    if (fn === 'seeded') {
      let x = (key ^ SEED) >>> 0;
      x = Math.imul(x, MULT) >>> 0;
      x = (x ^ (x >>> 15)) >>> 0;
      x = Math.imul(x, MIX) >>> 0;
      x = (x ^ (x >>> 13)) >>> 0;
      return (x >>> 16) % m;
    }
    const h = Math.imul(key >>> 0, MULT) >>> 0;
    return Math.floor(h / 65536) % m;
  }
  function makeKeys(pattern: string, fn: string, n: number): number[] {
    const keys: number[] = [];
    let x = 12345;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      if (pattern === 'random') { x = (Math.imul(x, 1664525) + 1013904223) >>> 0; keys.push(x); }
      else if (pattern === 'sequential') keys.push(i);
      else if (fn === 'poor') keys.push(i * 10);
      else if (fn === 'constant') keys.push(i);
      else keys.push(Math.imul(i, MULT_INV) >>> 0);
    }
    return keys;
  }
  function run(fn: string, pattern: string, n: number, m: number) {
    const lens = new Array<number>(m).fill(0);
    let insertProbes = 0, lookupProbes = 0;
    for (const k of makeKeys(pattern, fn, n)) { const b = bucketOf(fn, k, m); insertProbes += lens[b]; lens[b]++; }
    for (const l of lens) lookupProbes += (l * (l + 1)) / 2; // a lookup of the i-th key of a chain costs i probes
    return { lens, insertProbes, lookupProbes, total: insertProbes + lookupProbes, longest: Math.max(...lens), used: lens.filter((l) => l > 0).length };
  }
  function timeText(ns: number): string {
    if (ns < 1e3) return `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(ns)} ns`;
    if (ns < 1e6) return `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(ns / 1e3)} µs`;
    if (ns < 1e9) return `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(ns / 1e6)} ms`;
    if (ns < 6e10) return `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(ns / 1e9)} s`;
    return `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(ns / 6e10)} minutes`;
  }
  const hundredths = (a: number, b: number) => { const h = Math.floor((a * 100) / b); return `${formatThousands(Math.floor(h / 100))}.${String(h % 100).padStart(2, '0')}`; };

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ht]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = (s: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(s).value;
    const SVG = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
    function draw() {
      const fn = val('[data-fn]'), pattern = val('[data-pattern]');
      const n = Number(val('[data-n]')), m = Number(val('[data-m]')), cost = Number(val('[data-cost]'));
      const r = run(fn, pattern, n, m);
      const honest = run(fn, 'random', n, m);
      const avg = r.lookupProbes / n;
      q('[data-lf]').textContent = hundredths(n, m);
      q('[data-lfn]').textContent = `${formatThousands(n)} keys in ${formatThousands(m)} buckets: the expected chain length of a perfect hash`;
      q('[data-longest]').textContent = formatThousands(r.longest);
      q('[data-used]').textContent = `${formatThousands(r.used)} of ${formatThousands(m)} buckets used`;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-lbox]').style.setProperty('--c', r.longest <= 12 ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q('[data-avg]').textContent = hundredths(r.lookupProbes, n);
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-abox]').style.setProperty('--c', avg <= 3 ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q('[data-total]').textContent = formatThousands(r.total);
      q('[data-time]').textContent = `${formatThousands(r.insertProbes)} for the inserts and ${formatThousands(r.lookupProbes)} for the lookups; about ${timeText(r.total * cost)} at ${cost} ns per probe`;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-tbox]').style.setProperty('--c', r.total <= n * 5 ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      const chart = q<SVGElement>('[data-chart]');
      chart.textContent = '';
      const top = [...r.lens].sort((a, b) => b - a).slice(0, SHOWN);
      const w = 600 / SHOWN;
      top.forEach((v, i) => {
        const rect = document.createElementNS(SVG, 'rect');
        const h = v === 0 ? 1 : Math.max(2, (v / r.longest) * 98);
        rect.setAttribute('x', String(i * w)); rect.setAttribute('width', String(w - 1));
        rect.setAttribute('y', String(100 - h)); rect.setAttribute('height', String(h));
        rect.setAttribute('fill', v > 12 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
        chart.appendChild(rect);
      });
      q('[data-axis]').textContent = `The ${SHOWN} fullest buckets, left to right; the tallest has ${formatThousands(r.longest)} keys. Red: more than 12 keys in one chain.`;
      const ratio = r.total / honest.total;
      q('[data-dosn]').textContent = ratio === 1 ? 'same cost' : `${formatOneDecimalBelow100(ratio)} times`;
      q('[data-dost]').textContent = `random keys with the same hash and table cost ${formatThousands(honest.total)} probes (${timeText(honest.total * cost)}); this request costs ${formatThousands(r.total)} (${timeText(r.total * cost)})`;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-dos]').style.setProperty('--c', ratio > 3 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q('[data-verdict]').textContent = r.longest <= 12
        ? `The keys spread out: about ${hundredths(r.lookupProbes, n)} probes per lookup, so lookup cost does not grow with the number of keys.`
        : `Most keys share a few buckets: lookups walk chains of up to ${formatThousands(r.longest)} keys, so the cost grows with n and building the table with n².`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .ht-chart { width: 100%; height: 110px; display: block; background: var(--surface); border-radius: 6px; }
</style>
